id: migrations/2026-09-12-cohere-vocabulary-and-attribution
title: "Cohere the vocabulary, attribute the records, surface the decisions"
kind: migration-receipt
record_shape: header
status: active
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; changes proposed from JUDGMENTS.md and accepted by Dave in conversation; not a mass rewrite"
updated: 2026-09-12
supersedes: none
inventory_ref: JUDGMENTS.md

purpose: >
  Record what changed, what was deliberately left alone, and how to undo it.
  The judgment inventory of 2026-09-12 found the repository stating rules it
  did not enforce and enforcing rules it did not state. This receipt closes the
  gap by adding checks, not by rewriting history: every existing divergent value
  is grandfathered by file, every ledger may only shrink, and no record's
  meaning was changed.

what_changed:
  vocabulary:
    - change: "top-level status: closed to the lifecycle enum draft|active|superseded|archived|deleted"
      enforced_by: tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs
      grandfathered: "145 files, by name, frozen; ceiling 145; the ledger may only shrink"
      why: >
        38 distinct values were in use across 176 files, mixing lifecycle,
        version, authority, and loop position in one field the schema keeps as
        eight. templates/basic.yawn now teaches the enum on its status: line.
    - change: "authored_by: field with enum dave-human|agent-on-behalf|yawn.bot|unattributed and authored_via:"
      enforced_by: tests/authored-by.test.mjs
      required_on: [decisions/, dave/, records/yawn.bot-state.yawn]
      why: >
        100 of 194 .yawn files were last written by the yawn.ai git identity,
        which shares the maintainer's email; the tree could not say whether a
        stated preference was Dave's. The field says who is answerable.
    - change: "record_shape: declared in every template; templates/node.yawn ranks five shapes and names header canonical"
      enforced_by: tests/record-shape.test.mjs
      why: "four incompatible shapes with no statement of which was canonical"
  proof:
    - change: "proof: blocks must resolve every path they cite; covers: and not_covered: convention"
      enforced_by: scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs
      first_applied: core/canonical-extension.yawn
      why: >
        The canonical-extension proof named a validator that checks the alias
        list and nothing else, while the record also claims media_role and case.
        Its proof now says what it covers and lists the two claims it does not.
      grandfathered: "2 files citing a private Windows filesystem, by name, frozen; ceiling 2"
  manifest:
    - change: "yawn.yawn link tables kept complete against the filesystem"
      enforced_by: scripts/generate-manifest.mjs (check mode in npm run validate)
      applied: "54 missing links appended; no existing entry rewritten or removed"
  entities:
    - added: core/entity-and-coupling.yawn
      why: >
        Names the principal, the runtime, and a third entity whose name is held;
        defines the slash as a relationship record; carries the settled answer
        to the role question with its why and a recall rule.
  decisions:
    - added: decisions/
      count: "52 records from the reversal axes, numbered by leverage, plus 053 held"
      rule: "every record is proposed with an empty choice:; a recommendation carries authority: none"
    - added: records/yawn.bot-state.yawn
      generated_by: scripts/render-bot-state.mjs
      why: "a surface needs one record to read; the contracts said daily while the newest ledger entry was 2026-07-04"
    - added: dave/orientation/
      why: "the settled role drops from the top slot; the next highest-leverage question takes it"
  runtime_pointer:
    - change: "official_runtime.repository and agents/yawn.bot.yawn identity.repository corrected from yawn-ai/web-game to yawn-ai/yawn.bot"
      why: >
        Dave stated on 2026-09-12 that web-game is the older repository and is to
        be archived, and that yawn.bot with its Supabase database is the runtime.
        At the time of the change both repositories were at the same commit
        (a0ff2f4), so the correction is one of address, not content.
      epistemic_status: reported
      old_address_kept_as: superseded_repository
  entry:
    - added: CLAUDE.md
      why: "one file that is true on landing, for agents"
    - added: "CONTRIBUTING.md Attribution section and Authored-By commit trailer"
  validate_script: >
    npm run validate now also runs generate-manifest (check) and
    validate-proof-refs. CI runs npm test, which runs validate first.

not_migrated:
  - what: "the 145 grandfathered status: values"
    why: "rewriting them is a per-record judgment (is v0-seed draft or active?), not a mechanical one; each migrates when its record is next touched, and the ledger shrinks"
  - what: "the 15 references to C:/Users/dave/... in active records"
    why: "external workspace paths; renaming Dave's folder is not this receipt's to decide; the case and reachability questions are decisions/ records"
  - what: "record shapes of existing instances"
    why: "declared and ranked, not converted; a shape migration needs its own receipt with fixtures"
  - what: "the container entity's name"
    why: "held under core/canonical-extension.yawn creation_gate.on_ambiguity; decisions/053"
  - what: "the yawn.bot/dave dropdown and chat surface"
    why: "they live in the runtime repository; this receipt gives them one record to read"

rollback: >
  Every change is additive and lives in named files. Remove the four tests, the
  three scripts, and the two package.json validate steps and the previous suite
  passes unchanged. The 54 manifest links are appended at block ends and can be
  deleted as a range. record_shape:, authored_by:, and authored_via: lines can
  be stripped by a one-line filter. decisions/, dave/orientation/, CLAUDE.md,
  and core/entity-and-coupling.yawn are new paths. No record's prior content
  was rewritten except templates/basic.yawn (three header lines added) and
  core/canonical-extension.yawn (covers/not_covered added under proof:).

provenance:
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  merge_record: TAXONOMY.md
  holdout: HOLDOUT.md
  method: HOLDOUT_METHOD.md

proof:
  covers:
    - what_changed
    - not_migrated
    - rollback
  condition: "npm test passes on the tree this receipt describes, including the four new test files and the check-mode validators"
  tests:
    - tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs
    - tests/authored-by.test.mjs
    - tests/record-shape.test.mjs
  validators:
    - scripts/validate-proof-refs.mjs
    - scripts/generate-manifest.mjs
    - scripts/render-bot-state.mjs
  status: contract-defined
